      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486248206": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Role Type: Full-time\nLocation: Fully Remote\nExperience: 2–3 years\nCompensation: $700 USD base salary per month, plus up to $300 USD in performance-based bonuses per month.\nAbout the Role\nSmartPropFirm is looking for a Software Development Specialist to join our Product & Engineering team.\nYou'll build, maintain, and improve software products for the prop trading industry, including trading tools, customer dashboards, rewards systems, marketplaces, and other platform features.\nWe're looking for a skilled, proactive engineer with strong technical fundamentals, practical full-stack development experience, and the ability to independently solve problems, take ownership of features, and deliver reliable solutions using modern technologies and AI-assisted development tools.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain features across our web platform.\nBuild scalable, maintainable, and production-ready frontend and backend solutions.\nTake ownership of features from development through testing and deployment.\nIntegrate APIs, databases, authentication systems, and third-party services.\nIdentify and resolve bugs, performance bottlenecks, and technical issues.\nWrite clean, well-structured, reusable, and thoroughly tested code.\nConduct code reviews and contribute to improving engineering practices.\nLeverage AI development tools to accelerate development, debugging, and problem-solving.\nCollaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to deliver high-quality solutions.\nRequirements\n2–3 years of professional software development experience.\nStrong programming fundamentals and problem-solving skills.\nProficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Next.js, and Node.js.\nHands-on experience with full-stack web application development.\nSolid understanding of REST APIs, databases, authentication, and application architecture.\nExperience working with Git, code reviews, and collaborative development workflows.\nAbility to debug complex issues and optimize application performance.\nExperience using AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nStrong communication skills and the ability to work independently in a remote environment.\nAbility to take ownership of tasks and deliver high-quality work with minimal supervision.\nNice to Have\nFamiliarity with cloud services, CI/CD pipelines, and deployment workflows.\nUnderstanding of responsive UI/UX principles and frontend performance optimization.\nExperience with automated testing and production monitoring.\nExperience or interest in fintech, trading platforms, dashboards, marketplaces, or rewards systems.\nWhy Join SmartPropFirm?\nWork on real products used by traders.\nTake ownership of meaningful features and technical solutions.\nWork remotely with a collaborative, fast-moving team.\nBuild with modern technologies and AI-assisted development workflows.\nGain exposure to multiple products and complex engineering challenges.\nGrow professionally in an environment where your contributions have a direct impact.\nAdditional Requirements\n2-3+ years of hands-on experience with modern software engineering practices.\nStrong practical experience with Next.js and React.\nDemonstrated ability to independently develop, debug, and deliver production-ready features.\nComfortable working in a fully remote, collaborative development environment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486659480": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nQuora operates in the knowledge sharing and artificial intelligence space, addressing the challenge of organizing and distributing collective intelligence on a global scale. The organization provides two main platforms: a knowledge sharing site with millions of monthly users, and a cloud workspace for running AI agents collaboratively. This setup supports a wide user base and integrates multiple AI models, highlighting the company's emphasis on leveraging machine learning to enhance information access and collaboration.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER NEW GRAD, MACHINE LEARNING PLATFORM role focuses on developing and maintaining the infrastructure that supports large-scale machine learning models. This position contributes directly to the reliability, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems that serve hundreds of millions of users, enabling machine learning engineers to work more effectively. The role offers hands-on experience with distributed systems, GPU serving, and ML platform modernization, impacting the long-term success of the organization's core products.\nResponsibilities:\nBuild and maintain core infrastructure for the machine learning platform ensuring availability and scalability\nDevelop distributed systems for serving diverse machine learning models in production\nOptimize GPU model serving to improve latency, throughput, and cost efficiency\nContribute to platform standardization and modernization efforts\nCreate tools to enhance machine learning engineer productivity\nModernize feature store for faster feature deployment\nParticipate in on-call rotations to manage production issues\nRequirements:\nAvailability during coordination hours (Monday to Friday, 9am to 3pm Pacific Time)\nExpected 2025 or 2026 graduate in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field\nInterest in large-scale distributed systems and machine learning infrastructure\nFamiliarity or ability to learn Python, Go, or C++\nCommitment to continuous learning and team improvement\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nFor US-based applicants, the salary is $97,600\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical insurance\nVision insurance\nDental insurance\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487175455": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Company: Melcorsoft\nLocation: Lahore, Pakistan (On-site)\nEmployment Type: Full-time\nExperience: Fresh Graduate / 0–6 Months\nAbout Melcorsoft\nAt Melcorsoft, we build modern, scalable software products by combining strong engineering fundamentals with emerging AI technologies.\nWe believe the next generation of software engineers should be equally comfortable writing reliable code, solving complex technical problems, and leveraging AI to improve how software is designed, developed, and delivered.\nWe're looking for motivated, technically curious graduates who are passionate about software engineering, actively explore AI technologies, and want to build real-world products in a modern engineering environment.\nWhat You'll Do\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain scalable applications across frontend and backend systems.\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code following software engineering best practices.\nBuild RESTful APIs, integrate databases, and develop reusable application components.\nWork with modern technologies such as JavaScript, TypeScript, React, Next.js, Node.js, and Python .\nLeverage ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, or similar tools to assist with development, debugging, testing, and technical problem-solving.\nExplore and integrate AI capabilities using LLM APIs, structured outputs, tool calling, and automation workflows.\nEvaluate, debug, and refine AI-generated code to ensure correctness, performance, security, and maintainability.\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and collaborative problem-solving.\nResearch emerging AI technologies and identify practical opportunities to improve products and engineering workflows.\nTake ownership of assigned features from implementation through testing and delivery.\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n0–6 months of experience. Fresh graduates with strong academic, internship, or personal projects are encouraged to apply.\nSolid understanding of data structures, algorithms, object-oriented programming, and software engineering principles .\nProficiency in at least one programming language, preferably JavaScript, TypeScript, or Python.\nFamiliarity with frontend or backend development using frameworks such as React, Next.js, Node.js, or equivalent technologies.\nUnderstanding of REST APIs, HTTP, relational databases, and Git.\nBasic knowledge of debugging, testing, and writing maintainable code.\nHands-on experience with AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, or Claude Code , demonstrated through academic, personal, internship, or professional projects.\nUnderstanding of large language models (LLMs), prompt engineering fundamentals, and the practical capabilities and limitations of generative AI .\nAbility to independently understand, review, and troubleshoot code produced with AI assistance.\nStrong analytical thinking, problem-solving skills, and willingness to learn.\nPreferred Qualifications\nExperience building and deploying personal, academic, or internship-based full-stack applications.\nPractical exposure to OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, Gemini, or other LLM APIs .\nFamiliarity with AI application concepts such as RAG, embeddings, vector databases, function calling, or AI agents .\nExperience with Python-based AI application development or automation workflows.\nFamiliarity with PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or similar databases.\nBasic understanding of cloud platforms, CI/CD, automated testing, or containerization.\nActive GitHub portfolio, open-source contributions, hackathon experience, or independent technical projects.\nWhat We Value\nEngineering Excellence: You understand programming fundamentals, can reason about technical problems, and care about building secure, reliable, and maintainable software.\nAI Fluency: You have practical experience with modern AI tools, understand their strengths and limitations, and know how to incorporate them into effective development workflows.\nTechnical Curiosity: You actively explore emerging technologies, experiment with new approaches, and enjoy understanding how systems work under the hood.\nCritical Thinking: You don't blindly accept generated solutions. You question assumptions, validate outputs, and make informed engineering decisions.\nOwnership & Collaboration: You take initiative, communicate clearly, learn from feedback, and contribute meaningfully to team outcomes.\nWhy Join Melcorsoft?\nBuild real-world software products in an environment that combines modern software engineering with AI-driven innovation .\nWork with contemporary development technologies, AI-assisted engineering tools, and emerging LLM capabilities.\nLearn directly from experienced engineers through mentorship, code reviews, and hands-on development.\nGain practical exposure to full-stack development, AI integrations, system architecture, and production engineering.\nBe part of a team that values experimentation, technical excellence, continuous learning, and ownership.\nHow to Apply\nSend your updated resume along with your GitHub profile, portfolio, or links to relevant projects to hello@melcorsoft.com .\nWe're looking for engineers who can think independently, build confidently, and use AI intelligently.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487447757": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Purpose\n- Key Result Areas\n- Uses his/her technical expertise and experience to contribute to all sprint events (planning, refinements, retrospectives, demos)\n- Consults with the team about what is needed to fulfil the functional and non-functional requirements of the IT product to be developed\n- Develops the IT product, performs the unit test in line with the customer’s wishes and IT area’s internal ambitions and reviews colleagues’ IT products.\n- Designs, builds and tests IT products (functional, performance, resilience and security tests) and automates them.\n- Performs Life Cycle Management (including decommissioning) for IT products under management\n- Improves the Continuous Delivery process\n- Resolves incidents and problems relating to IT products under management (including stack)\n- Sets up the IT environment, deploys the IT product on the IT infrastructure and implements the required changes\n- Sets up monitoring of IT product usage by the customer\nOperating Environment, Framework and Boundaries, Working Relationships- The Front End developer is responsible for transforming the design and the product vision into working products and will directly influence how users will interact with the system. The Front End developer works hard to stay on top of fast changing technology and invests a lot of energy in learning new tricks. They are not only caught up on industry trends in client development frameworks but also know what the near future will bring. A love for clean interfaces and a passion for great user experiences goes without saying\n- Works within a multidisciplinary team or in an environment in which multidisciplinary teamwork is carried out.\n- Is primarily responsible for the production (or technical\nconfiguration) of software applications.\n- The range of tasks includes the following:\n- the analysis and design of the application(or the technical configuration);\n- coding applications and/or package integration in one programming languages, scripting languages and frameworks:\n- HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Continuous Delivery (Compile, Build, Package, Deploy);\n- Test-Driven Development (TDD) and test automation (e.g. regression, functional and integration tests); debugging and profiling;\n- software configuration management and version control.\n- Be an active participant in grooming and planning, to ensure that acceptance criteria are clear\n- Sit together with designers, SMEs and Product Owner while user stories are developed, bringing input\n- Work in an agile/scrum environment, meeting sprint commitments and contributing to the agile process\n- Maintain traceability of testing activities\nProblem Solving\n- Ability to handle challenges and multi-task, in a high pressure & demanding environment\nDecision Making Authority & Responsibility\n- Take ownership of key decisions, ensuring alignment with organizational goals and stakeholder expectations\nKnowledge, Skills and Experience\n- Past experience as a frontend developer building modern JavaScript-based web applications\n- Expert experience with HTML, CSS/LESS/SCSS/etc., JavaScript, and responsive design\n- Mobile development experience with either native or web-to-native tooling and frameworks\n- Experience using JavaScript frameworks and libraries specifically React\n- Understanding of RESTful APIs and how use them in practice\n- Knowledge of Object-Oriented programing\n- Ability to write effective unit, integration, and end-user automation tests\n- Strong understanding of Agile methodologies\n- Experience as a Developer on a cross-functional agile team preferred\n- Strong communication skills with ability to communicate complex technical concepts and align organization on decisions\n- Sound problem-solving skills with the ability to quickly process complex information and present it clearly and simply\n- Utilizes team collaboration to create innovative solutions efficiently\n- Passionate about technology and excited about the impact of emerging /\ndisruptive technologies\n- Wants to unleash inner self-starter and work in an environment that fosters\nentrepreneurial minds\n- Believes in culture of transparency and trust\n- Open to learning new ideas outside scope or knowledge skillset\n- Problem Analysis\n- Professional expertise/market focus",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488825431": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Role\nThe company is seeking an Entry-Level Software Engineer to join its fully remote team. This full-time position is designed for individuals beginning their software engineering careers who are interested in developing, maintaining, and improving software solutions under the guidance of experienced engineers.\nThe role involves writing clean and efficient code, contributing to back-end web services and APIs, participating in code reviews, and troubleshooting software issues. The selected candidate will also collaborate with cross-functional teams, document technical work, and support software testing and deployment activities while developing their technical skills in a distributed work environment.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain software solutions with guidance from experienced engineers.\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback to improve code quality.\nDebug software applications and identify and resolve technical issues.\nContribute to the development and maintenance of back-end web services and APIs.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to understand project requirements.\nDocument technical work and software development activities.\nAssist with software testing and deployment processes.\nLearn and adapt to new technologies, tools, and development practices.\nWork effectively with team members in a remote and distributed environment.\nRequired Qualifications\nFoundational knowledge of Computer Science, including algorithms, data structures, and software engineering principles.\nKnowledge of software development and programming, with experience in at least one modern programming language such as Java, C#, Python, or JavaScript.\nUnderstanding of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts and their practical application.\nExposure to back-end web development, including APIs, databases, and server-side frameworks.\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.\nAbility to work remotely, manage time effectively, and collaborate through online communication and project management tools.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nWillingness to learn, accept feedback, and develop technical skills through mentorship.\nPreferred Qualifications\nBasic knowledge of version control systems such as Git.\nUnderstanding of software development lifecycle practices.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4488827471": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Role\nWe are seeking an Entry-Level Software Engineer for a full-time remote position. Working under the guidance of experienced engineers, you will help design, develop, and maintain software solutions while building your technical skills and gaining practical experience.\nYour responsibilities will include writing clean and efficient code, participating in code reviews, debugging issues, and contributing to backend web services and APIs. You will also collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand project requirements, document technical work, and assist with software testing and deployment. This role is suited to someone beginning their software engineering career who is eager to learn, adapt to new technologies, and contribute in a distributed work environment.\nKey Responsibilities\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\nAssist in designing, developing, and maintaining software solutions.\nContribute to backend web services and APIs.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback from experienced engineers.\nDebug software and help identify and resolve technical issues.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to understand project requirements.\nDocument technical work and development activities.\nAssist with software testing and deployment processes.\nLearn and apply new technologies and software engineering practices.\nRequired Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.\nFoundational knowledge of computer science concepts, including algorithms, data structures, and software engineering principles.\nSkills in software development and programming, with experience in at least one modern programming language such as Java, C#, Python, or JavaScript.\nUnderstanding of object-oriented programming (OOP) concepts and their practical application.\nExposure to backend web development, including APIs, databases, and server-side frameworks.\nBasic knowledge of version control systems such as Git and software development lifecycle practices.\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\nWillingness to learn, accept feedback, and benefit from mentorship.\nAbility to work remotely, manage time effectively, and collaborate using online communication and project management tools.\nWork Arrangement and Employment Type\nEmployment Type: Full-Time.\nWork Arrangement: Remote.\nExperience Level: Entry-Level.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4489430743": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-12T00:50:03.220372+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "current openings\nWe are looking for\nFULL STACK WORDPRESS DEVELOPER\nFull Time\nkarachi, Pakistan\nResponsibilities\nSummary\nWe are looking for an exceptionally skilled Web Developer who is not just good at CSS3, HTML5, and JS but also has the ability/experience to work with PHP. The incumbent will be responsible for the execution of the following tasks:\nRequirements:\nProven experience as a Full Stack WordPress Developer or similar role.\nProficiency in front-end technologies like HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and front-end libraries/frameworks.\nStrong knowledge of PHP and experience in custom WordPress theme and plugin development.\nFamiliarity with database management and MySQL.\nExperience in integrating third-party APIs and services with WordPress.\nKnowledgeable in Adobe Photoshop, illustrator, premiere, and Mob App Development (Advantage)\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Web Development, or a related field (preferred)\nResponsibilities:\nDeveloping and working on User Interface (UI) design by using HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript & JQuery Design & developing websites that are cross-browsers, Cross Platforms, and Mobile Devices Compatible.\nWork with different content management systems.\nProactively perform cross-browser testing and optimizations for speed.\nIncorporating functionalities and features into websites\nMaintain well-documented, reusable, and transferable code.\nMaintains and updates WordPress websites.\nSkills:\nExperience in CSS3,\nHTML5,\nJavaScript\nJQuery skills,\nCode igniter, and WordPress.\nProficient in PHP (Core PHP & PHP framework).\nMinimum 6 months - 1 year of relevant Experience\nNote:\nPlease visit our website before Apply/Visit\nOur Website: https://quickdigitals.ae/\nSend your resume to this email:\nhr@quickdigitals.ae\nApply for this job\ncurrent openings\nDIGITAL MARKETING SALES EXECUTIVE\nDubai, UAE\nView Details Apply\nDIGITAL MARKETING EXPERT\nDubai, UAE\nView Details Apply\nSeo Technical Developer\nkarachi, Pakistan\nView Details Apply\nCONTENT WRITER\nkarachi, Pakistan\nView Details Apply",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
